1
00:03:05,454 --> 00:03:11,454
Part man, part machine, all cop.

2
00:06:10,909 --> 00:06:16,909
RoboCop is a action, thriller, science fiction film directed by Paul Verhoeven.

3
00:09:16,363 --> 00:09:22,363
In a violent, near-apocalyptic Detroit, evil corporation Omni Consumer Products wins
a contract from the city government to privatize the police force.

4
00:12:21,818 --> 00:12:27,818
To test their crime-eradicating cyborgs, the company leads street cop Alex Murphy into an armed confrontation
with crime lord Boddicker so they can use his body to support their untested RoboCop prototype.

5
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
But when RoboCop learns of the company's nefarious
plans, he turns on his masters.

6
00:18:32,727 --> 00:18:38,727
Officer Alex J. Murphy / RoboCop, played by Peter Weller.

7
00:21:38,181 --> 00:21:44,181
Officer Anne Lewis, played by Nancy Allen.

8
00:24:43,636 --> 00:24:49,636
The Old Man, played by Dan O'Herlihy.

9
00:27:49,090 --> 00:27:55,090
Dick Jones, played by Ronny Cox.

10
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
Clarence Boddicker, played by Kurtwood Smith.

11
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Bob Morton, played by Miguel Ferrer.

12
00:37:05,454 --> 00:37:11,454
RoboCop is a 1987 American science fiction action film directed by Paul
Verhoeven and written by Edward Neumeier and Michael Miner.

13
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:16,909
The film stars Peter Weller, Nancy Allen, Daniel O'Herlihy,
Ronny Cox, Kurtwood Smith, and Miguel Ferrer.

14
00:43:16,363 --> 00:43:22,363
Set in a crime-ridden Detroit in the near future, RoboCop centers on police officer Alex Murphy (Weller) who is murdered by a
gang of criminals and revived by the megacorporation Omni Consumer Products as the cyborg law enforcer RoboCop.

15
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
Unaware of his former life, RoboCop executes a campaign against crime while
coming to terms with the lingering fragments of his humanity.

16
00:49:27,272 --> 00:49:33,272
The film was conceived by Neumeier while working on the set of Blade
Runner (1982), and he developed the idea with Miner.

17
00:52:32,727 --> 00:52:38,727
Their script was purchased in early 1985 by producer
Jon Davison on behalf of Orion Pictures.

18
00:55:38,181 --> 00:55:44,181
Finding a director proved difficult; Verhoeven dismissed the script twice because he did not
understand its satirical content, until he was convinced of its value by his wife.

19
00:58:43,636 --> 00:58:49,636
Filming took place between August and October 1986, mainly in Dallas,
Texas with additional filming in Las Colinas and Pittsburgh.

20
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
Rob Bottin led the special-effects team in creating practical
effects, violent gore and the RoboCop costume.

21
01:04:54,545 --> 01:05:00,545
Verhoeven emphasized violence throughout the film, making
it so outlandish that it became comical.

22
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Censorship boards believed that it was too extreme and several scenes were
shortened or modified to receive an acceptable theatrical rating.

23
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
RoboCop was a financial success upon its release in
July 1987, earning $53.4 million.

24
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
Reviewers praised it as a clever action film with deeper philosophical
messages and satire, but were conflicted about its extreme violence.

25
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film was nominated for several awards, and won an
Academy Award and a number of Saturn Awards.

26
01:20:21,818 --> 01:20:27,818
RoboCop has been critically reevaluated since its release, and it has been hailed as one of the best
films of the 1980s and one of the greatest science fiction and action films ever made.

27
01:23:27,272 --> 01:23:33,272
The film has been praised for its depiction of a robot affected by the loss of humanity,
in contrast to the stoic and emotionless robotic characters of that era.

28
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:38,727
RoboCop has continued to be analyzed for its themes such as the nature of humanity, personal identity,
corporate greed and corruption, and is seen as a rebuke of the era's Reaganomics policies.

29
01:29:38,181 --> 01:29:44,181
Its success created a franchise: the sequels RoboCop 2 (1990) and RoboCop 3 (1993), children's animated series,
live-action television shows, video games, comic books, toys, clothing and other merchandise.

30
01:32:43,636 --> 01:32:49,636
A remake was released in 2014.

31
01:35:49,090 --> 01:35:55,090
The film explores themes of experiment, cyborg,
crime fighter, dystopia, giant robot.

32
01:38:54,545 --> 01:39:00,545
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
